WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.022
This activity combines a loop, several conditions, a counter, and readable output.

00:00:06.022 --> 00:00:13.147
A customer becomes priority when spending is at least two hundred fifty and visits are at least three.

00:00:13.147 --> 00:00:18.972
If that is not true but spending is at least one hundred, the customer is standard.

00:00:18.972 --> 00:00:21.273
Otherwise the label is follow up.

00:00:21.765 --> 00:00:24.707
Trace the three customers one at a time.

00:00:24.707 --> 00:00:27.442
Carla should meet the priority rule.

00:00:27.442 --> 00:00:33.452
Ava spends two hundred forty, so she does not reach the priority spending threshold.

00:00:33.452 --> 00:00:36.567
Ben falls into the follow-up category.

00:00:36.567 --> 00:00:39.227
Also notice the priority counter.

00:00:39.227 --> 00:00:43.224
It summarizes how many customers met the highest-level rule.
